## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design an EU-resident analytics flow with data governance, simple serverless components, and cost awareness.

## Key Concepts
- EU residency and data sovereignty
- Event-driven ingestion with Azure Event Hubs
- Serverless processing with Azure Functions
- Per-tenant access control via Cosmos DB RLS
- BYOK using Azure Key Vault
- Data retention and purge workflows
- DR planning and cost optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
module.exports = async function (context, eventHubMessages) {
  const { CosmosClient } = require('@azure/cosmos');
  const client = new CosmosClient(process.env.COSMOS_CONNECTION);
  const container = client.database('Analytics').container('TenantStats');
  for (const msg of eventHubMessages) {
    const payload = JSON.parse(msg.body);
    const item = {
      id: payload.id,
      tenantId: payload.tenantId,
      metric: payload.metric,
      value: payload.value,
      ts: new Date().toISOString()
    };
    await container.items.upsert(item);
  }
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle GDPR data deletion requests in this flow?
- What tests would you run to verify retention and DR requirements?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests building an observability-first, Azure-native pipeline with tenant isolation and simple DR, a common beginner-to-intermediate pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Event Hubs, Log Analytics, Azure Monitor, Application Insights
- Delta Lake on ADLS Gen2, per-tenant RBAC
- BYOK via Key Vault, basic DR to paired region
- Cost levers: retention, sampling, tiered storage

## Code Example
```javascript
// publish per-tenant logs to Event Hubs
const { EventHubProducerClient } = require('@azure/event-hubs');
const client = new EventHubProducerClient('<conn>', '<hub>');
async function send(tenantId, payload){
  const batch = await client.createBatch({ partitionKey: tenantId });
  batch.tryAdd(JSON.stringify({ tenantId, payload }));
  await client.sendBatch(batch);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-tenant RBAC across API, storage, and analytics views?
- What retention and cost controls would you apply to logs and metrics?
